e head of a tiny Internet-based commodities exchange."},{"id":"c04596d6-2375-47a8-a31c-10cf7753df2d","text":"Robert Willumstad left Citigroup in 2005 with ambitions to be a CEO."},{"id":"62eb9170-4a81-4888-afce-7fcfd23e6ca2","text":"He finally took that post at a major financial institution three years later."},{"id":"6241cc9a-4096-4a74-a478-b06df736ca4b","text":"Many recruiters say the old disgrace is fading for top performers."},{"id":"042261af-5684-4934-acc5-be2526598f0b","text":"The financial crisis has made it more acceptable to be between jobs or to leave a bad one."},{"id":"5b518cb3-2014-4243-a36a-ed7b7c8dbf21","text":"“The traditional rule was it’s safer to stay where you are, but that’s been fundamentally inverted,” says one headhunter."},{"id":"ab3d03f1-9e44-4358-aa8d-4d161464fd4a","text":"“The people who’ve been hurt the worst are those who’ve stayed too long.”"}],"currentSentenceIndex":0,"origin":"system"}'::jsonb,
