uicker turnarounds mean less wasted inventory, more frequent releases, and more profit."},{"id":"83a42db3-79b6-4cba-a1a2-721bec7675c5","text":"These labels encourage style-conscious consumers to see clothes as disposable – meant to last only a wash or two, although they don’t advertise that – and to renew their wardrobe every few weeks."},{"id":"7d9ca75c-7ccf-4aa1-a44b-a51b8ca4dbf0","text":"By offering on-trend items at dirt-cheap prices, Cline argues, these brands have hijacked fashion cycles, shaking an industry long accustomed to a seasonal pace."},{"id":"4ad2ef73-a186-4afa-a78b-5a3ad7470844","text":"The victims of this revolution, of course, are not limited to designers."},{"id":"e9b58c43-57fd-4dcc-a45d-404f17fca875","text":"For H&M to offer a $5.95 knit miniskirt in all its 2,300-plus stores around the world, it must rely on low-wage overseas labor, order in volumes that strain natural resources, and use massive amounts of harmful chemicals."},{"id":"d654bf15-c3de-4634-a464-c966337f9b43","text":"Overdressedis the fashion world’s answer to consumer-activist bestsellers like Michael Pollan’s TheOmnivore’sDilemma.","italicRanges":[{"start":0,"end":11},{"start":96,"end":116}]},{"id":"6fff557c-256a-4374-a836-767c281443f6","text":"“Mass-produced clothing, like fast food, fills a hunger and need, yet is non-durable and wasteful,” Cline argues."},{"id":"b3233458-0532-441a-ac4d-8188ba017da4","text":"Americans, she finds, buy roughly 20 billion garments a year – about 64 items per person – and no matter how much they give away, this excess leads to waste."},{"id":"19e46fdb-d06e-4181-a992-036d89ce89c0","text":"Towards the end of Overdressed, Cline introduced her ideal, a Brooklyn woman named Sarah Kate Beaumont, who since 2008 has made all of her own clothes – and beautifully.","italicRanges":[{"start":19,"end":30}]},{"id":"a1a78ddf-ae2c-4251-a616-949231930d06","text":"But as Cline is the first to note, it took Beaumont decades to perfect her craft; her example can’t be knocked off."},{"id":"8cc34757-0a8d-4be0-a85b-504a1b7ed2a5","text":"Though several fast-fashion companies have made efforts to curb their impact on labor and the environment – including H&M, with its green Conscious Collection line – Cline believes lasting change can only be effected by the customer."},{"id":"0c2d4302-43e0-4188-a448-26596ffb1a50","text":"She exhibits the idealism common to many advocates of sustainability, be it in food or in energy."},{"id":"b59ea29b-1a28-4625-a0be-574ec72d1020","text":"Vanity is a constant; people will only start shopping more sustainably when they can’t afford not to."}],"currentSentenceIndex":0,"origin":"system"}'::jsonb,
