ust be made of concrete benefits, such as approval of a contract or regulation."},{"id":"05d00d45-61bc-4a56-ac27-16cd5449f106","text":"Simply arranging a meeting, making a phone call, or hosting an event is not an “official act”."},{"id":"55c8f0b7-d950-4785-aa6d-f9f4bcfffe7d","text":"The court’s ruling is legally sound in defining a kind of favoritism that is not criminal."},{"id":"b7a06873-a0aa-4202-ab30-fceaf673495d","text":"Elected leaders must be allowed to help supporters deal with bureaucratic problems without fear of prosecution for bribery."},{"id":"41bd1840-01f5-40fc-a5df-df46dbff0b42","text":"“The basic compact underlying representative government,” wrote Chief Justice John Roberts for the court, “assumes that public officials will hear from their constituents and act on their concerns.”"},{"id":"44277844-d366-4b2c-a790-a7559340d6e0","text":"But the ruling reinforces the need for citizens and their elected representatives, not the courts, to ensure equality of access to government."},{"id":"0ada4249-638b-4d9e-acab-bba65a769413","text":"Officials must not be allowed to play favorites in providing information or in arranging meetings simply because an individual or group provides a campaign donation or a personal gift."},{"id":"8932eb48-e72c-4f0c-a425-fb2145652dd6","text":"This type of integrity requires well-enforced laws in government transparency, such as records of official meetings, rules on lobbying, and information about each elected leader’s source of wealth."},{"id":"01992253-3c92-4aa8-a88e-04ff7bc72708","text":"Favoritism in official access can fan public perceptions of corruption."},{"id":"8b58d3fe-eb32-4b41-a821-42b4a831a6fb","text":"But it is not always corruption."},{"id":"724cf3fb-7dd4-4ab8-af6c-8753f4a5460c","text":"Rather officials must avoid double standards, or different types of access for average people and the wealthy."},{"id":"843b71b8-c30e-4456-a053-efb451a48cca","text":"If connections can be bought, a basic premise of democratic society – that all are equal in treatment by government – is undermined."},{"id":"079897c8-b8bf-444c-a4a0-ae6c27fd521d","text":"Good governance rests on an understanding of the inherent worth of each individual."},{"id":"3a231034-8652-422f-a0de-159b00f5bece","text":"The court’s ruling is a step forward in the struggle against both corruption and official favoritism."}],"currentSentenceIndex":0,"origin":"system"}'::jsonb,
